- op: discuss  # a943
  at: '2026-09-28T03:23:12Z'  # a943
  by: agent  # a943
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a943
  clock: 3  # a943
  nonce: a943  # a943
  message: "Fixed in PR #1261 (ff7defd603). swift.yaml's Process subprocess row now carries run (instance and class forms share the name), launch and launchedProcess; launchPath (a property) is gone. objc.yaml's NSTask row gains launchedTaskWithLaunchPath:arguments: and launchedTaskWithExecutableURL:arguments:error:terminationHandler:. HIGH_RISK_PRIMITIVES follows. Behavioural evidence on merged dev, the item's own fixtures through hypergumbo io-boundaries --format json (cold cache): try p.run() -> subprocess Process.run; t.launch() -> Process.launch; try Process.run(u, arguments:) -> Process.run; Process.launchedProcess(...) -> Process.launchedProcess (all four were NO chain); [NSTask launchedTaskWithLaunchPath:arguments:] -> subprocess (was none). verify-claims {boundary: subprocess, must_not_exist: true} over a Swift program whose only launch is Process.run(u, arguments:) now returns violated (test_swift_objc_process_rows.py). CORRECTION to the filing's direction claim: before the fix that verdict was INCONCLUSIVE, not a false confirm -- the coverage gate caught the unclassified Process call ('calls into 1 module(s) ... (Process)'). io-boundaries itself reported nothing. A/B on real repos (pinned dev vs branch, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/proc_rows_09272026/): swift-argument-parser 4 and SwiftLint 2 chains move from Process.waitUntilExit to the Process.run in the same function; SwiftLint gains 2 launches in Source/swiftlint/Commands/Docs.swift (process.run() / process.launch()) that had no chain; vapor unchanged; no new chain lands on anything but Foundation.Process. NOT checked: whether an untyped receiver's .run() reaches the row (it should not: run is in swift ambiguous_names and the no-module gate withholds it)."  # a943
